## 3.5 Numbered Question Set Generation

Preserve the latest approved HOD question-set generation logic.

Do not reintroduce any earlier fixed-four or balanced-reuse implementation.

The current institutional rule is:

- The HOD configures the number of questions per module in one paper.
- The backend calculates the maximum number of complete numbered sets possible from the available valid question pool.
- Generate only that maximum number of sets.
- Every numbered set must have completely different questions.
- No Question ID can be reused across different numbered sets in the same generation.
- Do not generate incomplete sets.
- Do not fabricate questions.
- Do not assume exactly four sets.

The maximum set count must be calculated as:

Maximum Sets = minimum across configured modules of:

Floor(Available Valid Unique Questions in Module / Required Questions from Module per Set).

The HOD must NOT see the actual generated question composition of individual numbered sets.

HOD may see only:
- Number of sets generated.
- Questions per set.
- Module-wise distribution.
- Total unique questions allocated.
- Zero-overlap validation status.
- Publication status.

The HOD cannot see:
- Question-to-set mapping.
- Question texts belonging to individual generated sets.
- Options.
- Correct answers.
- Internal set allocation details.

All generation and publication data must come from the real backend.

Do not retain sample Set 1, Set 2, Set 3 or Set 4 records.

